🔸 What is AWS Cloud:-

AWS (Amazon Web Services) is a cloud computing platform offered by Amazon. It provides on-demand services like computing power, storage, databases, networking, machine learning, and security over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing.


---

🔸Key Benefits of AWS:-

Cost-effective: Pay only for what you use.

Scalable: Easily increase/decrease resources.

Reliable: Data centers around the world.

Secure: Strong data privacy and security features.

Global Infrastructure: 99 Availability Zones in 31 Regions (as of 2025).



---

🔸Core AWS Services:-

Here are some major AWS services grouped by category:

a. Compute

EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) – Virtual servers

Lambda – Serverless computing

Elastic Beanstalk – Easy app deployment


b. Storage

S3 (Simple Storage Service) – Object storage

EBS (Elastic Block Store) – Disk storage for EC2

Glacier – Archival storage


c. Databases

RDS – Relational DB (MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc.)

DynamoDB – NoSQL database

Aurora – High-performance DB


d. Networking

VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) – Private network in AWS

Route 53 – DNS and domain name service

CloudFront – Content delivery network (CDN)


e. Security

IAM (Identity and Access Management) – Manage users and permissions

KMS (Key Management Service) – Encryption key management

Shield – DDoS protection


f. Management Tools

CloudWatch – Monitoring

CloudTrail – Logging and tracking API calls

AWS Config – Configuration history



